  <running_head>Epist. 10. ad</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">4. Ejusmodi confœderationem ad-</l>
    <l n="2">mitti posse citra violationem juris Di-</l>
    <l n="3">vini, modo nihil inde decedat de pri-</l>
    <l n="4">vilegiis &amp; libertatibus Ecclesiarum par-</l>
    <l n="5">ticularium, nec infringantur jura col-</l>
    <l n="6">lata à Christo uni cuique Ecclesiæ</l>
    <l n="7">particulari, nec fides, nec disciplina in-</l>
    <l n="8">vitis obtrudantur.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">5. Quod quidem fieret, si inter il-</l>
    <l n="10">las Ecclesias uno confœderationis vin-</l>
    <l n="11">culo sic colligatas, tribunal Ecclesiasti-</l>
    <l n="12">cum supremum erigeretur, cujus dic-</l>
    <l n="13">tatis &amp; legibus, in fidei &amp; disciplinæ</l>
    <l n="14">negotio, tenerentur parere singuli cæ-</l>
    <l n="15">tus &amp; homines sub poena excommuni-</l>
    <l n="16">cationis, quemadmodum sancit dis-</l>
    <l n="17">ciplina nostrarum Ecclesiarum, Ca-</l>
    <l n="18">pit. 5. Artic. 31. titul. de Consistoriis.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">6. Eoque gravioribus incommodis</l>
    <l n="20">urgeretur ejusmodi tribunal, si ubi</l>
    <l n="21">diversitas religionis non obstat, non</l>
    <l n="22">daretur provocatio ad summum Ma-</l>
    <l n="23">gistratum, seu ad curias civiles.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">7. Sed grande crimen foret jurisque</l>
    <l n="25">alieni vendicatio &amp; occupatio, si in</l>
    <l n="26">territorio Magistratus, seu amici, seu</l>
    <l n="27">infensi, distinctum &amp; independens eri-</l>
    <l n="28">geretur</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword absent. Right margin word "geretur" is the end of the last line, printed at the right. Some words are damaged by stains (e.g. "fieret", "fidei"); readings are best guesses where the scan is worn.</notes>
